}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10x10, black background
  colors: input uses only black(0) and grey(5); output adds red(2)
  objects:
    count: 2 solid grey axis-aligned rectangles (4-connected)
    dimensions: each has height 3-6 and width 3-7, both >= 3
    fill: fully filled (area == h * w)
    placement: non-overlapping, separated by >= 1 row or >= 1 column of black
    border_touch: rectangles may touch grid edges [observed]
  transform:
    rule: recolor every interior cell (non-border) of each grey rectangle to red
    border: 1-cell grey border preserved on all sides
    interior_size: (h-2) x (w-2), always >= 1x1

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct (simple enough that forward construction works)
  steps:
    1. Create a 10x10 black grid.
    2. Generate two rectangles with h in [3,6] and w in [3,7].
    3. Place them on the grid such that they do not overlap and have >= 1 cell gap (no 4-adjacency between them). Allow edge-touching.
    4. Fill both rectangles entirely with grey.
    5. This is the input.
    6. For the output, copy input and recolor interior cells (excluding 1-cell border) of each rectangle to red.
```
